  "situation": "The AIB president must assess the evidence concerning an engine failure that destroyed an F-16CM and whether maintenance guidance substantially contributed to the mishap. Examination of the engine found two incorrectly installed stator vane sectors, one rotated 180 degrees from its designed position. Engineering analysis connected the vane configuration to pressure variations and vibration associated with compressor blade fatigue and failure. Maintenance records documented an inspection before installation of the upper forward stator case, while testimony described a stator sector falling out during installation; the records do not document that event or a subsequent inspection. Technical guidance warned that a vane sector could be installed incorrectly but did not detail how that could occur, and the warning appeared as a note. The applicable standards are clear and convincing evidence for determining the cause and a preponderance of evidence for determining contributing factors.",
